@page "/contact"
<PageTitle>Northstar Workshop | Contact</PageTitle>
<section class="contact-page">
    <div id="intro" class="page-intro">
<span class="badge text-bg-secondary">LET’S MAKE SOMETHING USEFUL</span>

<h2>Every good project starts with a hello.</h2>

<p>Tell us a little about your space, your plans, and what a successful outcome would look like. A rough idea is a perfectly good starting point.</p>
</div>
    <div id="contact-cards" class="card-grid">
<article class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>Bring your ideas</h3><p>A few photos, a sketch, or a short description are enough to get the conversation started.</p></div></article>

<article class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>Keep it practical</h3><p>Share your preferred timing and a comfortable budget range so we can suggest an appropriate next step.</p></div></article>

<article class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>No pressure</h3><p>The first conversation is about understanding the project and seeing whether we are the right fit.</p></div></article>
</div>
    <div id="contact-action" class="next-step">
<p>Sample contact link &#183; this fictional business does not receive messages.</p>

<a class="nav-link" href="mailto:hello&#64;example.com?subject=Northstar%20project%20enquiry">Open an email draft ↗</a>
</div>
    <div id="questions" class="faq-list">
<details><summary>Is this a real business website?</summary><p>This is an editable Blazor Studio sample. The company and service descriptions are fictional. No messages or personal information are stored.</p></details>

<details><summary>Can I edit this website in Studio?</summary><p>Yes. Open NorthstarWorkshop.csproj, then open a page under Components / Pages. Use Design to select text and cards, edit their properties, or add more tools.</p></details>
</div>
</section>
